// Kosher food — the certifier-directory set.
//
// Every place a recognised hechsher or Jewish community lists as kosher, drawn
// from 27 certifier and community directories (ORB, KLBD, OU, Star-K, the
// Queens and Five Towns Vaadim, COR, MK, Chabad and more). This is the breadth
// behind the curated highlights in kosher-eateries.ts.
//
// The rules are the same, and stricter here because the volume is larger:
//   • The hechsher is "reported", never "certified" — a directory listing is
//     not the owner confirming with the certifying body. The certifier is named
//     and linked, and the reader is told to confirm current supervision there.
//   • No diet is set. The directories list a place as kosher without saying
//     meat, dairy or parve, and guessing would be an invention. Absent means
//     "not stated by the source".
//   • No hours, no prices, no coordinates the source did not give. Navigate by
//     the address and confirm on the ground.
//
// Generated from data/imports/kosher-food-batch. Do not hand-edit; fix the
// source and regenerate.

